FEXCore on macOS, and cache generation with NoJIT (FEX 14c9268, on top of 0009)

macOS runs the same Darwin code as iOS (0007) and allows the same test
without an iPad, so the CMake checks accept CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME Darwin too.
The allocator shim tools link (JemallocDummy) uses <malloc/malloc.h>,
posix_memalign (also for aligned_alloc, which on Darwin
rejects sizes that are not a multiple of the alignment) and malloc_size on
Apple.

With NoJIT=1 a process can now also generate a cache: CompileBlock only
stops on a missing block while the guest runs, not while compiling blocks
for a cache, and the dispatcher FEX generates (and dumps for the AOT image)
is not made executable. That way the cache and dispatcher for the iPad are
made by a build with the same Darwin data layout, without executable memory.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 11eaf89..81248c5 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -61,9 +61,9 @@ if (NOT CMAKE_SIZEOF_VOID_P EQUAL 8)
   message(FATAL_ERROR "Unsupported pointer size ${CMAKE_SIZEOF_VOID_P}."
     " FEX only supports 64-bit (8-byte pointer) systems."
     " If you believe this is in error, file an issue.")
-elseif (NOT (WIN32 OR CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "Linux" OR CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "iOS"))
+elseif (NOT (WIN32 OR CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "Linux" OR CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "iOS" OR CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "Darwin"))
   message(FATAL_ERROR "Unsupported system type ${CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME}."
-    " FEX only supports Linux and Windows (and FEXCore on iOS)."
+    " FEX only supports Linux and Windows (and FEXCore on iOS and macOS)."
     " If you believe this is in error, file an issue.")
 endif()
 
@@ -78,8 +78,8 @@ elseif (MINGW)
   set(ENABLE_FEX_ALLOCATOR TRUE)
   set(ENABLE_JEMALLOC_GLIBC_ALLOC FALSE)
 elseif (APPLE)
-  # iOS: only FEXCore is built, for an app to link; the system allocator is used
-  message(STATUS "Building FEXCore for iOS")
+  # iOS and macOS: only FEXCore is built, for an app to link; the system allocator is used
+  message(STATUS "Building FEXCore for ${CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME}")
   set(ENABLE_FEX_ALLOCATOR FALSE)
   set(ENABLE_JEMALLOC_GLIBC_ALLOC FALSE)
 else ()
